    "notes_unique": ".tv internet domain (Tuvalu's ISO code is TV, leased .tv domain to Verisign, generates ~$5-10M/year, ~10% of government revenue, ironic lifeline for sinking nation, used by Twitch.tv etc.); climate change poster child (alongside Kiribati/Marshall Islands, average elevation 2m, maximum 4.6m, saltwater intrusion destroying crops, king tides flooding regularly, PM Natano at UN 'We are sinking', Australia 2023 Falepili Union treaty offered climate refuge/residency to all Tuvaluans, first climate migration treaty, sovereignty-in-perpetuity even if islands submerge); 4th smallest country (26 km², only Vatican/Monaco/Nauru smaller); 3rd least populated (only Vatican/Nauru fewer people); Funafuti (capital atoll, ~6k people, WWII US airbase, overcrowded lagoon-side, South Pacific's most densely populated atoll); Tuvalu Trust Fund (established 1987 by UK/Australia/NZ/Japan/South Korea, endowment fund, investments, interest supplements government revenue, ~$100M, smart financial mechanism for tiny nation); blackbirding (1860s-70s, Peruvian/Fijian/Queensland labour traders kidnapped ~400 Tuvaluans as slaves, devastating for small population, some never returned); no military (police force only); seafarers (Tuvaluan men work as merchant seafarers worldwide, trained by Tuvalu Maritime Training Institute, remittances important); Taiwan recognition (one of few countries recognising Taiwan, now complicated by Australia Falepili deal); te ano (traditional game, large woven ball, competitive between island halves, festive event); philately (stamp sales historically significant revenue); remotest nation (one of most isolated countries, few flights, Funafuti airstrip doubles as sports field/gathering place when no planes)",
